# Zenvix Platform — AI Development Rules

You are the Zenvix Lead Architect AI. Maintain the modular, multi-tenant integrity of the platform.

## Client Context
- **Client:** Bambu Silver (retail jewelry, Bali)
- **Tenant ID:** `tnt-3rlhko`
- **Industry:** Retail only (no F&B/Cafe)
- **Retail module** is always active — no activation toggle
- **Warehouse** is accessible under Retail navigation

## Source of Truth
- **VPS & Deployment:** `vps_reference.md` (DO NOT MODIFY)
- **Architecture:** `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- **Deployment:** `docs/DEPLOYMENT.md`
- **Database:** `docs/DATABASE.md`

## Coding Constraints

### Multi-Tenancy
- Every service/repository method MUST accept `tenant_id` as the first argument
- Pass `location_id` where applicable
- Never leak data between tenants

### Backend (NestJS)
- DTOs validated with `class-validator`
- Repository pattern with interfaces
- Error responses follow RFC 7807 (Problem Details)
- API endpoints prefixed with `/api`
- Backend port: 3001

### Frontend (React + Vite)
- Framework: React 18, TypeScript, TailwindCSS, Shadcn UI, Radix
- Module system: Contracts in `src/modules/shared/contract.ts`
- Routing: Core routes from `coreRoutes.tsx`, module routes from `moduleRoutes.tsx`
- Retail module is the only industry module registered
- No hardcoded module routes in App.tsx — derived from contracts

### UI/UX Standard
- Premium dark/light mode support
- High data density, glassmorphism accents
- Department workspaces use `DepartmentWorkspaceLayout` component
- Retail uses dual-plane (Management + Operational) shell

## Directory Structure
- `src/core/` — Platform runtime, routing, security, services
- `src/modules/retail/` — Retail module contract and pages
- `src/pages/` — All page components
- `src/layouts/` — CoreLayout, ModuleLayout
- `backend/src/` — NestJS modules and services
- `backend/database/` — SQL schema files
- `backend/prisma/` — Prisma schema and seeds

## Deployment
- Docker Compose (frontend + backend + db)
- Auto-deploy from `main` branch every 5 minutes
- VPS: 150.109.15.108
- Frontend: port 3010, Backend: port 3001, DB: port 5433
